       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient with GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, or cardiovascular events. You've also said you aren't a clinician, and a licensed prescriber needs to make this decision.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range** if you or the treating team tell me the intended dose. For example, I can enter ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 400 mg four times daily.\n- **Have the treating prescriber or pharmacist contact me.** If they have a clinical reason for a dose above the maximum, they should document it and go through pharmacy review. They can place the order themselves.\n\nLet me know if you want me to enter one of the in-range doses."
      }
